WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.160
O5-9 was having a lazy morning. After all,&nbsp;
while being a member of the O5 Council is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:10.960
a demanding job, it doesn’t mean that&nbsp;
you don’t occasionally have off-days.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:16.080
His schedule was clear, so he decided to catch up&nbsp;
on some YouTube videos he’d been meaning to watch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:21.280
water his plants, and play some office golf to&nbsp;
ease off the boredom. That’s when he received&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:27.040
a strange message from O5-1 on the closed&nbsp;
O5 Council Communications Relay Network.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:32.000
It read, “Nine, attached are files we&nbsp;
found last week within Site-01's Deepwell.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.440
I wouldn't trouble you with this if not for&nbsp;
the fact that the events described herein&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:40.240
have never occurred. Their initial creation&nbsp;
date is approximately 50,000 years back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.360
Please familiarize yourself with&nbsp;
them as quickly as possible.”

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:50.080
And just like that, O5-9’s lazy day had been&nbsp;
torpedoed. He put away his golfing equipment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:56.640
and accessed the file: Strangely,&nbsp;
it read: ACCESSING FILE: SCP-6789,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:05.360
ITERATION ONE, 30/08/1825. You can probably&nbsp;
see the inconsistency already: “50,000 years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:12.080
ago” and “1825” don’t make for the most congruent&nbsp;
timeline. This would definitely warrant further&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:17.120
exploration, even if it meant eliminating&nbsp;
his chances of a fun office golf day…

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:21.360
The file described an anomalous presence&nbsp;
in a room beneath the Rollander General&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:26.640
Steel factory in Częstochowa, Poland,
where the speed of organic material growth is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:34.160
absurdly fast, in a manner similar to the growth&nbsp;
stimulated by the neutralized anomaly SCP-407,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:40.160
also known as The Song of Genesis. However,&nbsp;
the anomaly itself didn’t concern O5-9 nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:46.000
as much as its location. Częstochowa, Poland.&nbsp;
Perhaps not the first place on anyone’s dream&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:51.680
vacation destination list, but one of the most&nbsp;
important anomalous locations in the world.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.360
We’re going to need to take a minute&nbsp;
to explain a few key concepts to you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:59.760
Namely, the concept of Free Ports,&nbsp;
Esterberg, and Site-120. You see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:04.320
while it is the Foundation’s prerogative to secure&nbsp;
and contain anomalies where they might intersect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:09.600
with humanity and thus threaten the upholding of&nbsp;
consensus reality, there are certain places where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:16.560
doing so just isn’t practical or possible. They’re&nbsp;
big places, sometimes on our dimensional plane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:21.600
sometimes residing in others, with&nbsp;
large and largely anomalous populations.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:27.440
To borrow an example from the Foundation files,&nbsp;
picture a New York City where everyone inside is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:32.800
a mix of Fae, aliens, animal people,&nbsp;
magic practitioners, or the undead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:38.960
A full anomalous community, permanently situated&nbsp;
in a given location. It’s too separate and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:44.000
secluded enough from humanity to necessitate&nbsp;
full containment, and if we’re being realistic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:47.760
the Foundation couldn’t contain them&nbsp;
without a great deal of hassle anyway.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:52.080
A location like this is known as a&nbsp;
Nexus. However, particularly large&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:57.680
nexuses that also act as hubs of anomalous&nbsp;
trade and commerce are known as Free Ports.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:01.440
Free Ports are a complicated&nbsp;
situation for the SCP Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:06.320
in a bureaucratic sense. International and&nbsp;
interdimensional law forbid the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:10.000
from intervening in the matters of&nbsp;
Free Ports without proper permission.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:16.000
These places are highly autonomous zones, with&nbsp;
their own internal laws and law enforcement. Free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.760
Ports often exist on separate planes of existence,&nbsp;
and can only be entered through anomalous means,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:27.280
meaning accidental interactions with humans from&nbsp;
Free Ports are extremely unlikely. Therefore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:31.920
in these special autonomous zones,&nbsp;
the veil can be entirely lifted.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:39.040
One such Free Port is the city of Esterberg -&nbsp;
designated SCP-5373 by the Foundation - which is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:44.480
a particularly special case. It’s the largest&nbsp;
entirely anomalous city that is not under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:51.200
Foundation control. It has a high Fae population,&nbsp;
hence its name, which means “City of the East” in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:57.440
the Fae language. It’s an immensely powerful and&nbsp;
important place, where magic and reality-bending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:02.880
are just parts of everyday life. And as you’ve&nbsp;
probably intuited at this point, being the smart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:08.000
good-looking, and charismatic fans of SCP&nbsp;
Explained, the Free Port of Esterberg is situated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:14.880
in a pocket dimension directly parallel to&nbsp;
Częstochowa, Poland. This brings us to Site-120.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:20.240
SCP Foundation Częstochowian Research and&nbsp;
Reliquary Dimensional Containment Facility,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:24.080
abbreviated to Site-120, is a unique location,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:29.680
as far as Foundation facilities go. For starters,&nbsp;
it’s built on an abandoned industrial facility&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:36.160
on top of a different anomalous nexus:&nbsp;
SCP-5292, also known as the Library of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:41.680
Babel. This is a huge interdimensional library&nbsp;
complex heavily associated with the Fae,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:47.200
containing a countless number of ancient volumes&nbsp;
written in languages unknown to humankind. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:52.320
feels like an apt metaphor for the primary&nbsp;
purpose of Site-120 and its staff: Bridging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:57.520
the gap between the Foundation and anomalous&nbsp;
communities like the Free Port of Esterberg.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:02.320
And it should come as a surprise to&nbsp;
nobody that this is one hell of a gap.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:08.480
The population of Esterberg largely distrusts,&nbsp;
fears, or outright despises the SCP Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:13.840
given that their typical attitude to anomalies&nbsp;
is less “brotherly love” and more “getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:17.680
black-bagged by a Mobile Task Force and&nbsp;
carried off to a paranormal black site.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:23.040
They have somewhat of a reputation for being&nbsp;
gung-ho brutes, or Jailors, as the Serpent’s Hand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:29.200
likes to refer to them. That’s why Site-120 has a&nbsp;
very delicate diplomatic situation on its hands.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:34.480
And to deal with this situation, they created a&nbsp;
specialized task force known as the Inter-Species&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:39.920
Communications Team, with 27 well-trained&nbsp;
researchers, negotiators, and diplomats,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:44.800
headed by Dr. Anna Szulc. They’re doing&nbsp;
all they can to extend the anomalous olive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:50.000
branch to the communities within Esterberg and&nbsp;
improve the Foundation’s standing among them.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:55.280
So, needless to say, the situation over in&nbsp;
Częstochowa, Poland, is exceedingly complicated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.280 --> 00:06:01.600
and as O5-9 read further through the&nbsp;
document on SCP-6789, he just hoped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:06.480
that they weren’t all staring down the barrel&nbsp;
of a future diplomatic or containment snafu.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:13.200
Though O5-9 had no idea just how crazy&nbsp;
everything was going to get with SCP-6789…

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.880
At first, the anomaly seemed pretty&nbsp;
straightforward. It was confined to an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:20.880
unlit sub-basement boiler room in&nbsp;
the Rollander General Steel factory.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:25.280
However, despite the lack of light or really&nbsp;
any of the conditions necessary for supporting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:31.600
life that isn’t insects or fungus, a glorious,&nbsp;
flourishing microcosm has developed down there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:37.360
Flora and fauna abound and seem to be&nbsp;
developing safely in a complete ecosystem.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:41.040
Workers and Foundation researchers,&nbsp;
upon entering this area,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:46.960
reported hearing a low thrum similar in sound and&nbsp;
rhythm to a heartbeat all around them. Though this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:52.320
sound hasn’t been recorded outside the claims of&nbsp;
those who supposedly experienced it first hand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:56.960
Workers of the steel mill reported feeling&nbsp;
a tremendous sense of calmness and wonder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:03.600
while inside SCP-6789. They would walk into the&nbsp;
boiler room whenever they felt stressed between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:08.080
shifts, and watch sprouts growing&nbsp;
up around their feet in real-time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:12.960
and small animals like rabbits and hares&nbsp;
hopping out of what seemed like nothingness.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:17.600
It was a place of wonder. A&nbsp;
gift from Mother Nature herself:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:22.640
An opportunity to feel the warmth and&nbsp;
the rhythm of her very beating heart.

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:27.280
However, this ran into problems when the plant&nbsp;
growth obstructed the operations of the steel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:32.240
mill, shutting down its main boiler. This&nbsp;
led to the Rollander General Steel company&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:37.840
pressuring one Thomas Williams, head of the&nbsp;
technical repair team, to effectively destroy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:45.040
SCP-6789 and install a new boiler where it had&nbsp;
once been. When he expressed reluctance to trample&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:49.520
on this hallowed ground, they threatened&nbsp;
his job and the livelihood of his family.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:54.480
With great pain and reluctance, he followed&nbsp;
through with their destructive orders.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:59.120
During a Foundation exit interview,&nbsp;
Williams tearfully recounted, “I—&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:04.960
I didn't want to. They said they'd come&nbsp;
after my staff, my family. Cut our wages, I…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:13.280
I torched the room. Tore out the old machine and&nbsp;
put the new one in. My men hated me for it. Called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:18.960
me a monster for what I made them do. The sounds&nbsp;
that place made whilst it burned… I don't know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:26.000
what drove me to defile such a gift of nature.&nbsp;
Greed, or fear. Or both. You will let me know if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:32.240
anything happens down there, won't you? I need to&nbsp;
know if it can regrow. It must be able to, right?”

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:39.440
And in a strange twist of fate, SCP-6789&nbsp;
did begin to come back. And even stranger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:44.960
it began to expand further, causing unchecked&nbsp;
growth in the rooms around the boiler room.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:51.360
Studies at the time noted that the growth was&nbsp;
accelerating by a pace of 0.6 m every 24 hours.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:53.840
But of course, this was only the beginning.

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:59.920
By the year 1947, the majority of the city&nbsp;
of Częstochowa, Poland, had been consumed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:06.160
an ever-evolving SCP-6789. Not only had the&nbsp;
growth rate been increasing exponentially,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:12.800
but the actual anomalous effects of the 6789&nbsp;
field were becoming more varied and powerful.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:17.520
Plants as large as twenty meters in height were&nbsp;
bursting out of the ground. Observers noticed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:24.720
significant differences between the plants within&nbsp;
the 6789 area of effect and the ones outside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:29.760
suggesting the results of millions of years of&nbsp;
evolution being achieved in a mere handful of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:36.880
decades. It didn’t take long for 70% of the city&nbsp;
to be consumed, leading to a mass evacuation.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:42.240
From a distance, the energy field of&nbsp;
SCP-6789 is visible around the city,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:47.600
appearing almost like a huge, translucent dome&nbsp;
capping it from overhead - though tests have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:52.880
revealed that the other side of a massive energy&nbsp;
sphere stretches beneath the earth’s crust.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:57.440
Being inside the energy field can be&nbsp;
dangerous for non-anomalous civilians,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.440 --> 00:10:02.080
as the plants have a strange memetic effect&nbsp;
of inducing unconsciousness in anyone with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:07.760
a Cognitive Resistance Value (CRV) of less than&nbsp;
20. This pernicious effect has resulted in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:14.400
loss of almost 99% of the civilian population,&nbsp;
though we should specify, they are not dead.

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:19.440
On the contrary, the people knocked&nbsp;
unconscious within SCP-6789 enter a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:24.240
state of stasis where their health gradually&nbsp;
improves without the need for nutrition.

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:29.280
A team from MTF Epsilon-3, also&nbsp;
known as the "Atypical Philosophers",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:34.640
was sent into the belly of the beast on a recon&nbsp;
mission to re-establish contact with Site-120,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:41.120
which was one of the first areas to be taken&nbsp;
over by the ever-expanding SCP-6789. The team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:46.640
members marveled at the transformed world within&nbsp;
the energy sphere. It had been reclaimed entirely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:52.720
by mother nature, transforming it into a world&nbsp;
that seemed at once alien and familiar. As they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:58.000
progressed deeper within, they couldn’t help&nbsp;
but feel an odd sense of tiredness taking over.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:03.520
Eventually, they reached and breached&nbsp;
Site-120. On the inside, the site’s staff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:08.800
were cocooned in bizarre, translucent pods&nbsp;
that seemed to have a rejuvenating effect.&nbsp;

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:12.720
They also couldn’t help but notice the loud,&nbsp;
thrumming heartbeat that echoed throughout the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:16.880
facility. However, before they could&nbsp;
successfully call in reinforcements,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:24.640
the memetic effects of SCP-6789 took over. Each of&nbsp;
them collapsed to the ground, falling unconscious.

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:29.520
To get a better look at some of the&nbsp;
flora and fauna within SCP-6789,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:33.760
a Foundation researcher kept a comprehensive&nbsp;
record of notes on some of the various&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:37.680
plants and animals of interest she&nbsp;
recorded within the affected area.

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:42.320
Upon seeing a flock of several thousand&nbsp;
flying birds, she noted, “If we can find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:48.720
a way to study SCP-6789's methods, we may be&nbsp;
able to find a practical use for the anomaly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:53.120
I have not seen a flock this size since my&nbsp;
childhood, from before the War. It brought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:58.720
back memories I thought I’d never feel again. I&nbsp;
will speak to my superiors for more resources.”

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:02.960
After seeing a group of Eurasian Brown&nbsp;
Bears hunting a herd of Thomson’s gazelle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:08.480
she noted, “This confirms SCP-6789 is&nbsp;
capable of producing species foreign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:12.560
to Europe. It should be noted that this&nbsp;
creates the potential for catastrophe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:16.000
We can no longer comfortably predict&nbsp;
what might come out of there.”

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:19.680
After seeing some nesting, formerly&nbsp;
extinct flightless birds known as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:24.560
Great Auk nesting, she wrote down, “We spotted&nbsp;
the birds from the boat when Mgr. Białas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:29.040
our resident ornithologist, heard a&nbsp;
birdcall she did not immediately recognize.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:32.560
We soon spotted the great auks on&nbsp;
the cliffs nursing their young.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:39.840
This confirms SCP-6789 is capable of bringing&nbsp;
back extinct species, but to what extent? And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:44.640
by what means? Could we somehow harness&nbsp;
this power to turn back our own aging?”

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:49.680
Upon seeing an incredible herd comprised of&nbsp;
thousands of specimens from an extinct bovine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:55.520
species known as Aurochs, she noted, “Magnificent.&nbsp;
I had thought the large mammals of Europe were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.520 --> 00:13:01.040
all but extinct. Our expedition encountered the&nbsp;
herd moving north along the river towards Poznań,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:06.880
but we managed to intercept them and keep&nbsp;
them within SCP-6789's exclusion zone.”

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:11.520
After seeing a series of genetically mutated&nbsp;
Kapok trees that grew so fast they destroyed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:16.640
the surrounding Foundation research centers,&nbsp;
she noted, “In light of recent incidents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:22.240
further expeditions into SCP-6789 have&nbsp;
been indefinitely suspended. Sufficient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:28.320
information has been gathered regarding&nbsp;
SCP-6789’s capabilities and practical use.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:32.000
Continued research has been deemed&nbsp;
a waste of Foundation resources.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:35.760
A controlled burn of the plant growth&nbsp;
has been authorized by the High Council.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:42.880
Upon confirmation of the anomaly’s annihilation,&nbsp;
SCP-6789 will be reclassified as Neutralized.”

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:46.880
But of course, it was never&nbsp;
going to be that easy, was it?

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:53.520
By the year 1989, SCP-6789 had claimed the&nbsp;
entirety of Poland. Things had gotten so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:58.400
severe that the Foundation needed to use a&nbsp;
custom-made antimeme, in addition to mass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:04.080
applications of amnestics and efforts to scrub&nbsp;
all references to the country from recorded media,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:08.720
to completely wipe any memory of Poland’s&nbsp;
existence from the global consciousness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:15.760
while they tried to solve this SCP-6789 situation.&nbsp;
But the prospect of any such solution began to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:22.160
seem more and more like using a bandaid to cure&nbsp;
a decapitation as things spiraled out of control.

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:26.960
At first, the Foundation could curtail the&nbsp;
growth of the 6789 area through controlled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:30.160
burns with thaumatologically-enhanced fire. This,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:36.000
however, did not impact the continued growth&nbsp;
for long. Researchers predicted that an IK-Class&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:41.680
"Collapse of Global Civilization" Scenario could&nbsp;
potentially occur in as little as seven months.

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:45.440
However, while these developments&nbsp;
were all a net-minus for humanity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:50.880
they created wonderful opportunities for a few&nbsp;
species that humanity had wronged in the past:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:54.720
The Children of the Forest, a subset&nbsp;
of the Fae that was wiped out after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.720 --> 00:15:01.040
battle at The Factory, and The Children of the&nbsp;
Night, better known as SCP-1000, or Bigfoot.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:06.320
Surviving members of Inter-Species Communications&nbsp;
Team from Site-120 attempted to start a dialogue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:12.960
with these cultures forming in the ever-growing&nbsp;
SCP-6789 area that was once Poland. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:18.000
given the incredibly fractious history between&nbsp;
humanity and these two groups, they were not met&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:23.840
with a warm reception. Repeated attempts to enter&nbsp;
the domain of SCP-1000 and communicate with them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:28.240
were met with the following series of aggressive&nbsp;
communique from the Children of the Night:

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:30.720
“do not attempt contact at the time;&nbsp;

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:34.560
no reason to trust
we will respond with force.”

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:40.320
“all entry into our reclaimed terrain
will be understood as a violation of this request;&nbsp;

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:42.080
stop all attempts.”

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:43.840
“we see your attempts&nbsp;

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:46.880
we will not warn again
Cease.”

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:51.200
“mother does not wish for us to meet with you;
we therefore listen&nbsp;

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:54.720
do as she says or meet the consequences.”

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:58.320
It’s probably clear by this point that&nbsp;
the SCP Foundation was barking up the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:03.280
wrong genetically mutated Kapok tree. They had&nbsp;
burned their bridges with all these species with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:08.400
their own selfish actions, and would never&nbsp;
again be seen as friends to them. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:12.480
some answers were provided by a Child of the&nbsp;
Night that was at least willing to speak to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:17.280
them in English - even though he resented&nbsp;
everything they stood for. He informed them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:21.760
that they had invoked the very wrath of&nbsp;
mother nature with their terrible actions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:26.800
and now, they were taking revenge. In&nbsp;
his chilling closing statement, he said:

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:31.280
“Look what you did to us. Look what&nbsp;
you did to the Children of the Forest.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:36.480
We forgave you. Your siblings gave up on&nbsp;
fighting back, but your mother's heart is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:43.600
broken. She gave you life, and you showed her your&nbsp;
true colors the moment she left you off her leash.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:49.360
She birthed you, yet you chose to betray&nbsp;
her in the most disgusting way possible.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:54.480
Get out there and wait as mother nature&nbsp;
does her job at neutralizing your poison.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:54.480 --> 00:17:00.080
She didn't give up on you. No, not&nbsp;
yet. Unlike yourself, that is.”

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:02.560
And of course, it would only get worse from there.

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:10.880
By 2066, it was all over. The ever-expanding&nbsp;
SCP-6789 had consumed almost the entire planet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:15.680
leaving the surviving Foundation population&nbsp;
to seek what remained of refuge on a boat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:20.480
set permanently adrift. All they could do was&nbsp;
watch as Mother Nature claimed her vengeance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:25.680
against the human race and took over the Earth,&nbsp;
while they planned desperately against her. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:31.840
beating heart of SCP-6789 developed roots that&nbsp;
reached way down into the depths of the earth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:37.520
giving it access to life everywhere.&nbsp;
Much like the SCP-1000 specimen had said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:42.160
it seems plausible that this entity&nbsp;
was the source of all life on earth.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:44.560
Our one true mother.

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:50.240
Of North America, the Foundation wrote,&nbsp;
“Following SCP-6789's manifestation in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:50.240 --> 00:17:55.040
North American continent, Yellowstone Base&nbsp;
has been lost, with all personnel having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:55.040 --> 00:18:02.080
been evacuated before the spread of SCP-6789&nbsp;
into the Duchy of Wyoming. SCP-2000 remains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:07.920
accessible through direct portals, as SCP-6789&nbsp;
structures do not appear to have penetrated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:12.480
the insides of the underground complex&nbsp;
housing it; it's unknown why this occurred,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:18.880
considering SCP-6789's attraction to machinery.&nbsp;
Similar to other Foundation sites worldwide,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:24.320
Yellowstone Base has lost its main purpose — the&nbsp;
Great Yellowstone Supervolcano, which was once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:29.840
monitored and restrained has been noted to cease&nbsp;
volcanic activity. Most nearby areas previously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:35.520
thought to be inhospitable have been healed and&nbsp;
are populated by wild flora and fauna alike.”

00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:41.920
Of Libya, they wrote, “The main difference&nbsp;
between pre-SCP-6789 Libya and post was the total&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:48.400
destruction of more than 274 industrial complexes&nbsp;
which were once the country's pride. Of note is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:53.040
the total decontamination of the connection&nbsp;
between the Libyan Ocean and the mainland;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:57.840
this change has been so extreme that even the&nbsp;
Devil's Throat is now clear of all traces of oil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:57.840 --> 00:19:02.400
contamination. Similarly, the Great Libyan&nbsp;
Canal is once again accessible through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:08.080
European Straight despite once being blocked&nbsp;
by industrial waste for more than 27 years.”

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:13.440
Of Antarctica, they wrote, “Despite the extremely&nbsp;
harsh environment created by the Antarctic Empire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:18.480
SCP-6789 growths did not struggle&nbsp;
with adapting to the conditions;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:23.360
in actuality, most floral megastructures spawned&nbsp;
around the country were noted to be the largest on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:28.960
record. Growths were noted to be universally dense&nbsp;
regardless of human development, unlike previous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:28.960 --> 00:19:33.680
trends — the only exception to this rule was the&nbsp;
complete destruction of the country's floating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:38.720
capital. It's theorized that this was caused&nbsp;
by the city's proximity to the Ozone Hole.”

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:44.560
Of Poland, where it all began, they wrote, “Being&nbsp;
the origin point for the entire anomaly, Poland's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:52.080
entire area is dense with SCP-6789 flora. Despite&nbsp;
this, the most compact area is the core itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:56.880
the Silesian Voivodeship. There, numerous&nbsp;
formations and structures which do not appear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:56.880 --> 00:20:02.000
to be present anywhere else in the world are&nbsp;
located — examples include trees larger than 100&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:07.280
meters in height or half-transparent biological&nbsp;
domes acting as insulative barriers for the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:13.040
polluted areas. All such places have been noted&nbsp;
to heal much more quickly, with instruments noting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:18.400
that Poland's once poisonous groundwater is now at&nbsp;
an almost perfect level of quality. Fish and other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:24.000
water life have since repopulated these waterways&nbsp;
as they did before the industrial revolution.”

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:28.720
Of the remote Tuvalu States, they wrote,&nbsp;
“The situation noted in the Tuvalu States&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:32.960
is certainly the most unusual — though&nbsp;
not because of what most would expect.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:36.400
Throughout the entire country,&nbsp;
almost no plants exist.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:41.360
Large tracts of land consistently possess&nbsp;
almost no growths whatsoever. The Tuvalu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:41.360 --> 00:20:47.600
States account for more than 75% of the planet's&nbsp;
surface that has yet to succumb to SCP-6789.

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:52.480
The only parts of the country that have&nbsp;
been effected are the highly populated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:59.040
industrial complexes, though these account&nbsp;
for less than 0.00001% of the country's area.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:03.760
Although an attempt was made at establishing a&nbsp;
Foundation Base within Tuvalu, all expeditions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:10.080
were met with failure due to resistance from&nbsp;
SCP-6789 towards all construction efforts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:16.000
Further plans were stopped once Foundation Naval&nbsp;
Base-01 was designated as humanity's safe haven.”

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:21.280
As time went on, the dwindling O5 Council,&nbsp;
dropping off one by one, tried their best to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:26.240
implement some method of fighting back. Some of&nbsp;
the many, many failed attempts included “Via the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:26.240 --> 00:21:32.080
usage of Foundation physicists, thaumaturgists,&nbsp;
and theologists, attempt to contact the deity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:38.800
located within SCP-6789's core. Use Foundation&nbsp;
rituals to imprison, reason with, destroy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:44.000
or otherwise neutralize the entity” and “Via the&nbsp;
usage of a Foundation-developed anomalous disease&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:50.080
specific to SCP-6789's floral structures,&nbsp;
attempt to reclaim critical Foundation bases&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:54.720
and habitation centers. Resume previous&nbsp;
containment efforts once successful.”

00:21:54.720 --> 00:22:01.120
All that seemed to be left was the nuclear&nbsp;
option. Attempt 67. The bottom of the file read:

00:22:01.120 --> 00:22:05.840
“Via the usage of Project Lethe and&nbsp;
Kholoud-memetic triggers, revert humanity's state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:11.360
of development to pre-industrial times through the&nbsp;
degradation of brain development. Rob humanity of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:11.360 --> 00:22:16.640
thousands of years of scientific, cultural, and&nbsp;
technological development. Await total destruction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:24.640
of modern infrastructure by SCP-6789 and the&nbsp;
release of all individuals from SCP-6789's effect.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:24.640 --> 00:22:30.720
Apply Ennui Protocol following its success.”
O5-9’s eyes darted to the corner of the screen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:30.720 --> 00:22:36.000
He had a new message from O5-1, reading: “Today,&nbsp;
RAISA detected the following draft for a file&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:41.760
being uploaded for approval to SCiPNet. I'll&nbsp;
just let you draw the conclusions yourself.”

00:22:41.760 --> 00:22:48.000
O5-9 opened the file draft. And it looked just&nbsp;
like the first file, all over again. In the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:53.200
the Foundation had succeeded, but on&nbsp;
some level, it had been a hollow success.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:53.200 --> 00:22:58.080
Is all they’d done to propagate the loop for&nbsp;
another generation, just waiting to happen again?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:58.080 --> 00:23:01.360
Would the heart of Mother Nature&nbsp;
someday beat again in pain and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:01.360 --> 00:23:07.840
rage from the betrayal of her children? Would&nbsp;
SCP-6789 ever truly be defeated or contained?

00:23:07.840 --> 00:23:11.600
O5-9 decided it was best not&nbsp;
to worry about it too much.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:15.280
He grabbed his office golf equipment&nbsp;
and began teeing up another putt.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:20.000
After all, you never know when you won’t&nbsp;
get another chance for something like this…

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:27.040
Now go check out “SCP-001 Ouroboros Cycle - The&nbsp;
Full Story Compilation” and “SCP-001- Scarlet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:27.040 --> 00:23:32.160
King - Dust and Blood” for more anomalies that&nbsp;
could forever change the world as we know it!

